.\" Manual page for overlay-timer
.TH OVERLAY\-TIMER 1 "November 2026" "overlay-timer 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
overlay\-timer \- translucent, click\-through countdown and pomodoro overlay timer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B overlay\-timer
.RB [ \-t
.IR TIME ]
.RB [ \-\-pomodoro
.IR N ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B overlay\-timer
.RB { \-\-pause | \-\-resume | \-\-stop }
.br
.B overlay\-timer
.RI [ appearance\ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B overlay\-timer
draws a translucent text counter on top of all windows, without receiving
focus or clicks (click\-through), fixed in one of the four corners of one or
more screens. It supports a simple
.B countdown
mode and a
.B pomodoro
mode.
.PP
When invoked to start a timer, the process forks into the background
(daemonizes) and returns the terminal immediately. Only a
.B single instance
runs at a time. Further invocations talk to the running instance over a Unix
domain socket to reconfigure, pause, resume, stop, or move the overlay.
.PP
In
.B countdown
mode the timer counts down from a given time; upon reaching zero it blinks and
plays a long sound. In
.B pomodoro
mode it runs
.I N
work blocks (default 25 min) separated by breaks (default 5 min, shown in
green). The end of each work block or break plays a short beep; the last work
block has no break after it and plays the long sound while blinking.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Time / mode
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time " " \fITIME\fR
Start a countdown. \fITIME\fR is \fBMM:SS\fR or \fBHH:MM:SS\fR (a bare number is
seconds).
.TP
.BR \-\-pomodoro " " \fIN\fR
Start \fIN\fR pomodoros.
.TP
.B \-\-sync
Only with \fB\-\-pomodoro\fR. Align the pomodoro cycle (work + break) with the
system clock, anchored at local midnight. With the default 25 + 5 minutes this
means work blocks start at \fB:00\fR and \fB:30\fR of every hour. If started
during a work block, the first pomodoro gets only the time remaining (e.g. at
\fB:02:20\fR it starts with \fB22:40\fR); if started during a break slot
(e.g. \fB:28:10\fR), the session begins with the break of "pomodoro 0"
(\fB01:50\fR) and all \fIN\fR pomodoros follow.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fBhhmmss\fR | \fBmmss\fR
Display format. The actual time value takes precedence (if hours are present,
they are shown).
.SS Appearance
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-color " " \fICOLOR\fR
Text color: a known name (\fBred\fR, \fBgreen\fR, \fBblue\fR, ...) or
\fB#RRGGBB\fR / \fB#RGB\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-alpha " " \fI0\-100\fR
Visibility of the text (0 = fully transparent, 100 = opaque).
.TP
.BR \-\-size " " \fI0\-100\fR
Text size as a percentage of the screen's smaller dimension.
.TP
.BR \-\-font " " \fIFAMILY\fR
Font family (fontconfig name). Empty = system default.
.TP
.BR \-\-corner " " \fBtl\fR | \fBtr\fR | \fBbl\fR | \fBbr\fR
Corner: top\-left, top\-right, bottom\-left, bottom\-right.
.TP
.BR \-\-screen " " \fIIDX\fR[,\fIIDX\fR...]
Screen index(es). The same timer is replicated on each chosen screen.
.SS Pomodoro
.TP
.BR \-\-pomodoro\-minutes " " \fIM\fR
Duration of each work block, in minutes (default 25).
.TP
.BR \-\-break\-minutes " " \fIM\fR
Duration of the short break, in minutes (default 5).
.TP
.BR \-\-long\-break\-minutes " " \fIM\fR
Duration of the long break, in minutes (default 15).
.TP
.BR \-\-long\-break\-every " " \fIN\fR
Insert a long break after every \fIN\fR pomodoros. 0 disables long breaks
(default).
.TP
.BR \-\-pomodoro\-color " " \fICOLOR\fR
Text color during work blocks.
.TP
.BR \-\-break\-color " " \fICOLOR\fR
Text color during breaks.
.SS Control (requires a running timer)
.TP
.B \-\-pause
Pause the running timer.
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Resume the running timer.
.TP
.B \-\-stop
Stop the running timer and remove the overlay.
.SS Audio
.TP
.BR \-\-sounds\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Directory holding the \fB.wav\fR files
.RB ( timer_end.wav ", " pomodoro_end.wav ", " break_end.wav ).
Missing files fall back to a synthesized triangular tone.
.TP
.BR \-\-sound ", " \-\-no\-sound
Enable or disable sound.
.SS Window system
.TP
.BR \-\-x11 ", " \-\-wayland
Force the X11 or Wayland backend. By default the backend is auto\-detected from
.BR XDG_SESSION_TYPE ", " WAYLAND_DISPLAY " and " DISPLAY .
The Wayland backend requires the
.B wlr\-layer\-shell
protocol (Sway, Hyprland and other wlroots compositors). Compositors without
it (e.g. GNOME/Mutter) are not supported and produce a clear error.
.PP
On macOS the native AppKit backend is always used (config value
.BR backend " = " macos ).
On Windows the native Win32 backend is always used (config value
.BR backend " = " win32 ).
.SS Config
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Use an alternate configuration file instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-\-save
Merge the current options into the configuration file and write it.
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOR
If a timer is already running, control flags
.RB ( \-\-pause ", " \-\-resume ", " \-\-stop )
and appearance/position overrides are sent to the running instance, which
reconfigures itself. Attempting to start a new timer
.RB ( \-t " or " \-\-pomodoro )
while one is running is an error: stop the current one first with
.BR "overlay\-timer \-\-stop" .
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from an INI file, by default
.IR ~/.config/overlay\-timer/config.ini
(or
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/overlay\-timer/config.ini ).
It is created with defaults on first run. Command\-line options override the
file; use
.B \-\-save
to persist them. Sections and keys:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[appearance]  color, alpha, size, font
[position]    corner, screen
[timer]       format
[pomodoro]    pomodoro_minutes, break_minutes, long_break_minutes,
              long_break_every, pomodoro_color, break_color
[audio]       sounds_dir, enable_sound
[window]      backend
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/overlay\-timer/config.ini
Configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/overlay\-timer/sounds/
Default directory for the \fB.wav\fR sound files.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/overlay\-timer/log
Log file (defaults to \fI~/.local/state/overlay\-timer/log\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/overlay\-timer.sock
Control socket for the single running instance.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/overlay\-timer.lock
Lock file enforcing a single instance.
On macOS, where
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
is not set, both files live in
.IR $TMPDIR/overlay\-timer/ .
.PP
On Windows the configuration file is
.IR %APPDATA%\(rsoverlay\-timer\(rsconfig.ini ;
the log and the control socket live in
.IR %LOCALAPPDATA%\(rsoverlay\-timer\(rs ,
and a named mutex replaces the lock file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_TYPE\fR, \fBWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fR, \fBDISPLAY
Used to auto\-detect the window system backend (ignored on macOS and Windows).
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Standard XDG base directories, used for config, sounds, logs and the socket.
.TP
.B LC_ALL\fR, \fBLANG\fR, \fBLANGUAGE
Select the interface language (English and Brazilian Portuguese are provided).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error (e.g. no running timer, backend failure).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start a 25\-minute countdown:
.B overlay\-timer \-t 25:00
.TP
Run four pomodoros, green text, top\-right corner:
.B overlay\-timer \-\-pomodoro 4 \-c green \-\-corner tr
.TP
Pause and later resume the running timer:
.B overlay\-timer \-\-pause
.br
.B overlay\-timer \-\-resume
.TP
Move the overlay to the top\-left corner and save it:
.B overlay\-timer \-\-corner tl \-\-save
.TP
Stop the timer:
.B overlay\-timer \-\-stop
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg\-user\-dirs (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for the overlay\-timer project.
